## SQ-CS-09 | Fruits Delight apple sapling merges into Vinery's; no Fruits Delight apple trees
@group server
@commands `/give @s fruitsdelight:apple_sapling`; new world, `/locate biome minecraft:flower_forest`, fly over 10 chunks; grep latest.log `[itemMerges]`
@pass the sapling becomes Vinery's apple tree sapling; no Fruits Delight apple trees; merge count line includes the creativedelight pairs
@fails biome modifier override not loaded, or merge group skipped by `requires: vinery`
@from batches/r1031/b1_gameplay.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> give qa fruitsdelight:apple_sapling
> data get entity qa Inventory
> execute positioned 0 70 0 run locate biome minecraft:flower_forest
waitlog nearest minecraft:flower_forest is at 300
capture FF is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> tp qa {FF1} 200 {FF3}
sleep 30
> cdevtest count {FF1-48} 40 {FF3-48} {FF1+48} 140 {FF3+48} fruitsdelight:apple_leaves
expect verb=count block=fruitsdelight:apple_leaves n=0 
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
reject fruitsdelight:apple_sapling
bootexpect \[itemMerges\]
look the inventory shows the Vinery apple sapling id; the leaves count is 0 with skipped_columns well below 9409 (the box was loaded); the [itemMerges] boot line count includes the creativedelight pairs

